<title>USA: Amdahl Q4 shr loss $0.28 after charge.</title>
<headline>Amdahl Q4 shr loss $0.28 after charge.</headline>
<dateline>SUNNYVALE, Calif. 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>AMDAHL CORPORATION</p>
<p>   FOURTH QUARTER ENDED     Dec 27, 1996	   Dec 29, 1995</p>
<p> Revenues		   $    491,848,000    $     416,180,000</p>
<p> Income (Loss) Before Taxes (32,891,000)	   (35,766,000)</p>
<p> Net Income (Loss)	    (33,890,000)	   (38,366,000)</p>
<p> Average Shares Outstanding  121,370,000	    119,116,000</p>
<p> Net Income (Loss) Per Share	 (.28)		    (.32)</p>
<p>   YEAR ENDED		   Dec 27, 1996	   Dec 29, 1995</p>
<p> Revenues			1,631,549,000	  1,516,388,000</p>
<p>Income (Loss) Before Taxes</p>
<p>				   (313,682,000)	     49,977,000</p>
<p> Net Income (Loss)	   (326,682,000)	     28,527,000</p>
<p> Average Shares Outstanding  120,510,000	 120,383,000(a)</p>
<p> Net Income (Loss) Per Share	(2.71)		   .24(a)</p>
<p>NOTE: (a)Fully Diluted.</p>
<p>Year 1996 includes Q2 charges of $20.7 million to write off in-process R&amp;D and $130 million to write down certain processor assets. Also Q4 1996 includes a $40 million charge, or $0.33 per share, for restructuring expenses. Combined, the 1996 charges equal approximately $1.58 per share.</p>
<p>Year 1995 includes Q4 charges of about $27.3 million to write off in-process R&amp;D and $26 million to write down certain inventories. The charges equal about $0.44/shr.</p>
</text>
